course: dictionary
lesson: 9077
title: Slope: going up and down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A slope is ground or a surface with one end higher than the other, like a hill. You meet the word in parks, on ski trips and in science lessons. «The garden slopes down to the river.» The word slopes tells you the garden goes down towards the water, so it is not flat.
explain: Slope can also be a noun, a thing, or a verb, a doing word. Context tells you which. «Ski slopes» are hills used for skiing, so slope is a thing there. In «The garden slopes down», slopes is what the garden does. Ask: what does the sentence show? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Steep and gentle describe slopes. A steep slope rises or falls very sharply, while a gentle slope is easy to walk up. Words like «slippery slope» are different again: it is a phrase, not a hill, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A slope is a surface that goes up or down, with one end higher than the other.
fact: To slope means to go up or down at an angle.
fact: «Ski slopes» are hills used for skiing.
fact: In science, a slope is a simple machine, like a ramp: things roll faster down a steeper slope.
fact: In maths, slope means how steep a line is.
exercise: «The garden slopes down to the river.» What does slopes mean here? | Is covered in bright flowers | Stays perfectly flat | Shines in the sun | * Goes down at an angle
exercise: In «You can burn even on a ski slope», what is a ski slope? | A kind of umbrella | A ski lift with a seat | A cold wind over the snow | * A hill used for skiing
exercise: In science, what is a slope? | A type of rock | A kind of weather | * A simple machine, like a ramp
test: Which describes a steep slope? | * Very sharp, hard to climb | Covered with grass only | Flat as a table | Easy to walk up
test: In «A slippery slope says one small step will lead to disaster», what does slippery slope mean? | * An idea that one small step leads to bigger trouble | A wet hill covered in mud | A slope for sledging | A ramp used for science
exam: Riya says a slope in maths is a hill for skiing. What does slope mean in maths? | A kind of shelf | A type of paint | * How steep a line is | Ski hill
